---
description: Spontus implementation workflow
alwaysApply: true
---

Build one feature slice at a time.

Required reading before coding:
1. docs/README.md
2. docs/domain-glossary.md
3. docs/product/mvp-overview.md
4. docs/product/domain-model.md
5. docs/product/mvp-build-slices.md
6. docs/product/ux-walkthrough.md
7. docs/engineering/development-readiness.md
8. docs/engineering/tech-stack.md
9. docs/figma-map.md
10. docs/implementation-plan.md

MVP build order:
1. Team profile foundation
2. Sponsor profile and listing foundation
3. Team application flow
4. Sponsor review flow
5. Manual verification and admin workflow

Implementation rules:
- Prefer TypeScript and explicit data types.
- Keep mock data structured like the future database model.
- Reuse components rather than duplicating screen-specific UI.
- Keep manual verification status in the MVP.
- Keep messaging lightweight; do not build a full chat product early.
- Do not add unrequested features.
- Do not implement payments, escrow, AI contracts, advanced analytics, full CRM, or automated matching in the first MVP slice.

After coding:
- Run lint/typecheck/tests when available.
- Summarize changed files.
- Note any deviations from Figma.
- Note any product questions or open decisions.
- Suggest the next smallest slice.
